you're going to see

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:38.284
very faintly that number.

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:40.987
72, that is the USS Abraham Lincoln

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:44.090
talking about preparations In the U.S.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.458
Navy has sent out

00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:47.660
ten ships from the Third Fleet

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:50.463
just to minimize ship

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:51.430
overcrowding

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:54.233
because the waters were very choppy here.

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:56.269
So preparation was key

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:59.238
damage minimal in the city of San Diego.

00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:00.673
This is the wettest

00:09:01.741 --> 00:09:02.808
weather event for

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:05.978
San Diego since 1873 when President Grant

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:06.913
was in the White House.

00:09:06.913 --> 00:09:09.749
So certainly a bullet dodged.

00:09:09.949 --> 00:09:11.984
Victor and Poppy Victor.

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:12.852
Very sorry.

00:09:12.852 --> 00:09:14.520
It's before the crack of dawn.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.022
So we will certainly wait

00:09:16.022 --> 00:09:17.757
until the sun comes up

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:18.991
to assess the rest of the damage.

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:19.926
But it seems as though

00:09:19.926 --> 00:09:21.994
our friends in the desert communities

00:09:21.994 --> 00:09:23.896
have faced the brunt of this storm

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:25.231
and have the worst of the damage.

